  "name": "Callboard quests fill the cache progress bar and a full bar pays the released stage's cache",
  "contract": "Callboard Cache progress. The client asks a quest's points with CMSG 0x731 (quest id) and reads SMSG 0x732 (quest id, points, 0); captured live replies (questcacheaddon.wdb, 2026-08/09) give Dungeon Diving 81244 15 and the world boss quest 170015 50, and uncaptured quests follow the Bronzebeard video of 2025-11-05: profession 15, world kill 20, elite 25. A quest outside the Callboard is worth 0. At login the server sends SMSG 0x730 with one cache record (count 1; id, 0, condition 0, item level 0, cache item, points per cache) and the TOKEN_TYPE_CALLBOARD_CACHE_POINTS token (SMSG 0x670: name, amount, 0). At the default release stage 7 the cache is Callboard Cache (Naxxramas) 1615009, and one cache costs 150 points. A turn-in adds its points and pays one cache per 150, keeping the remainder: four elite quests reach 100, two world kill quests 140 with no cache yet, and a profession quest 155, which pays one cache and leaves 5. The points survive the next login.",
